# hsk py check

## Cooperative lock

Before running any `hsk py ruff-sort-docs` / `hsk py check` cycle (including linked projects), use the lock file at `.cursor/hsk-py-check.flag`.

Only the **first non-empty line** matters (trim whitespace, case-insensitive). Lines below it are human hints; do not parse them. Do not commit this file.

Modes:

- `idle` — no check running; next agent may take the lock and run the **incremental** cycle (`--only-changed`)
- `full` — no check running; next agent may take the lock and run the **full** cycle (no `--only-changed`)
- `busy` — a check cycle is running; other agents wait and re-read
- `skip` — do not run `hsk py ruff-sort-docs` / `hsk py check`

Protocol:

1. Read the first non-empty line of `.cursor/hsk-py-check.flag` (if the file is missing, treat as `idle`).
2. If the mode is `skip`: do **not** run `hsk py ruff-sort-docs` or `hsk py check` (including for `harrix-pylib` / `harrix-pyssg`). State in the reply that checks were skipped because of `skip`. Exception: an **explicit** user request to run the checks overrides `skip` for that request — take the lock as usual (use incremental unless the user asked for a full run).
3. If the mode is `busy`: wait 15–30 seconds (`sleep` / `AwaitShell`), then re-read. Do not busy-loop tool calls without a pause. If `busy` for longer than **10 minutes**, treat the lock as stale (`idle`) and take it (the previous agent may have crashed).
4. If the mode is `idle`, `full`, missing, or unknown: remember the available mode (`full` stays `full`; missing/unknown → `idle`), write the file with first line `busy` and keep the same comment block as the template, then run the matching check cycle.
5. Whoever wrote `busy` must restore the remembered available mode (`idle` or `full`) at the end — on success, after 3 failed iterations, and on environmental failure. Preserve the comment block. Do **not** overwrite `skip` or `full` if the user set that mode while you were waiting or running (if you started from `idle` and the file now says `skip`/`full`, leave it).
6. When writing the file, use this shape (first line is the current mode):

```text
busy

# hsk py check lock — only the first line is the mode
# idle — available; run ruff-sort-docs --only-changed + check --only-changed
# full — available; run ruff-sort-docs + check (full tree / full suite)
# busy — a check cycle is running; other agents wait and re-read
# skip — do not run hsk py ruff-sort-docs / hsk py check
```

(Replace the first line with `idle` or `full` when releasing; user may set `skip` or `full` manually.)

## Check cycle

After completing code changes, run this cycle from the project root (with venv active).

### Incremental (`idle`, default)

1. `hsk py ruff-sort-docs --only-changed`
2. `hsk py check --only-changed`

`--only-changed` limits format/sort/docs and checks to Git working-tree-changed files (ty/ruff/Harrix on dirty `.py`/`.md`, pytest on related tests).

### Full (`full`)

1. `hsk py ruff-sort-docs`
2. `hsk py check`

Use this when the flag is `full`, or when the user explicitly asks for a full-tree rebuild / full-suite verification.

There is no `hsk py ruff` command. Use `hsk py ruff-sort --only-changed` only when docs generation is not needed; prefer `ruff-sort-docs` (with or without `--only-changed`, per mode) before `check`.

If `hsk` fails with `Access is denied` on `hsk.exe` (often because the app is running from the same venv), close the app or run the equivalent checks via `python -m` (`ruff`, `ty`, `pytest`) and still report that the full `hsk py check` could not complete.

Fix until the chosen `hsk py check` variant passes. Repeat this cycle up to **3 times maximum**. If it still fails after 3 iterations, stop and report the remaining errors.

Do not finish while the chosen check still fails, unless the failure is environmental and cannot be fixed in code.

## Cross-project check

Linked external projects:

- `harrix-pylib`
- `harrix-pyssg`

Run the same cycle as the flag mode (`--only-changed` for `idle`, full commands for `full`) in an external project **only if that project itself was modified** in this session. Do not check unmodified linked projects.

If an external project was modified: fix until the chosen check passes there (up to **3 times maximum**), unless the failure is environmental and cannot be fixed in code.
